        "original_id": "e4f556b5-fbb5-54aa-af74-4fd84e0dce94",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Maharashtra Gramin Bank, Regional Rural Banks, Government of India Ministry of Finance Department of Financial Services\n- Concepts: amalgamation, rural banking, basic banking and financial services\n\nFacts:\n- On 20 July 2009, the Government of India Ministry of Finance Department of Financial Services issued notification F.No 1/4/2006-RRB(II).\n- On 20 July 2009, Maharashtra Gramin Bank came into existence after the amalgamation of Maharashtra Godavari Gramin Bank and Marathawada Gramin Bank.\n- Regional Rural Banks are local-level banking organizations that operate in different states of India.\n- Regional Rural Banks were created primarily to serve rural areas of India with basic banking and financial services.",
